USB Audio Class 1 playback
==========================

This sample is a standalone Circle audio device with stereo PWM output.
It advertises unsigned 8-bit PCM (ALSA U8), signed 8/16/24/32-bit PCM and 32-bit float at 32, 44.1 and 48 kHz.
The USB device connector must be available to the DesignWare gadget controller;
use a supported gadget-capable board and the Circle gadget configuration.
The output uses the board's normal PWM sound routing (analog jack where present).
A Zero without an analog jack needs suitable PWM output hardware; this sample
does not control the BioSynth I2S DAC, ADC or Pico.

Build the Circle core, USB, input, fs, sound and usb/gadget libraries, then run
make here. See doc/usb-audio-gadget.md for the architecture and limitations.

Before building, set USB_GADGET_VENDOR_ID and USB_GADGET_DEVICE_ID_AUDIO
in Config.mk using DEFINE += -D... for each value. Use IDs authorized for
your device. Circle's default vendor ID is zero and initialization refuses it.

After loading, select UAC1 Playback on the host. Start at low amplifier volume.
The sample adapts USB audio to a fixed 48 kHz PWM output using a simple linear
resampler. Prefer 48 kHz for comparisons; it is not a reference-quality SRC.
Master mute and volume controls are supported. Counters are logged every five
seconds. Callbacks and processing are bounded; no audio logging runs in IRQ.

Diagnostics are available on the UART at 115200 baud; HDMI is optional.
